# TV Doctor settings for your own TV and network.
#
# Copy this file to .env (in the project folder, or ~/.config/tvdoctor/.env)
# and fill in your values. .env is git-ignored, so your TV's details stay on
# your machine. Every value is optional: leave one blank and TV Doctor works it
# out (discover finds the TV, the subnet comes from this laptop's address).
#
# Wi-Fi details are never needed. TV Doctor only has to be on the same network
# as the TV; it does not read, store or send your Wi-Fi name or password.

# The TV's IP address on your network. Find it with: tvdoctor discover
# (or on the TV: Settings > Network > About). --ip on the command line wins.
TVDOCTOR_IP=

# The first three parts of your network's addresses, for discover to sweep,
# e.g. 192.168.1 or 10.0.0. Only needed if discover scans the wrong network
# (say, when on a VPN).
TVDOCTOR_SUBNET=

# Extra apps to protect from bloat and clean --deep, comma separated.
# TVDOCTOR_KEEP=com.showmax.app,com.plexapp.android
TVDOCTOR_KEEP=

# Port for the TV Doctor window on this laptop (http://127.0.0.1:PORT).
TVDOCTOR_PORT=8787
